  "id": "DrugBank_DB14491 - MONDO_1860",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Fumarate is being considered for repurposing in the treatment of Folic Acid Deficiency Anemia, based on its association with anemia and hematin formation. The evidence suggests that Ferrous Fumarate may influence the development of anemia by promoting hematin production, which is a precursor to Folic Acid Deficiency Anemia. This pathway is supported by multiple indirect indications, where Ferrous Fumarate is linked to anemia and hematin, which in turn are associated with Folic Acid Deficiency Anemia. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the direct mechanism linking Ferrous Fumarate to Folic Acid Deficiency Anemia remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a potential role of Ferrous Fumarate in the pathogenesis of this condition, though further mechanistic studies are needed to confirm the exact mechanism.",
